From: sunfish-gpu
Subject: [PATCH] SweetFramebuffer: kern.sweetfb_fit / boot-arg sweetfb_fit: the presented display shrunk 24/25 onto the panel, whole

The panel showed the centre of the presented 1125x2436 display at full size: 22 columns
cut off at each side, 48 rows at the top and the bottom. With sweetfb_fit the whole display is
shrunk onto the panel's 1080 columns (24 of 25, as the iPhone 12 mini shows 1125x2436 on
1080x2340): of each 25 columns and rows the 13th and 14th are averaged, the rest copied.
Touch follows (SweetHID.cpp). Off by default; switch at run time with the sysctl.
---
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c	2026-10-27 15:12:11.591027170 +0200
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c	2026-10-27 15:12:11.602249272 +0200
@@ -98,6 +98,14 @@
 int sweet_fb_gpu_waits = -1;    /* -1: the boot-arg's (SweetFramebuffer.cpp sets it at start) */
 SYSCTL_INT(_kern, OID_AUTO, sweetfb_gpuwait, CTLFLAG_RW | CTLFLAG_LOCKED, &sweet_fb_gpu_waits, 0,
     "the display waits for the GPU before it shows a swap");
+/*
+ * kern.sweetfb_fit=1: the presented 1125x2436 display is shrunk by 24/25 onto the 1080 columns of
+ * the panel, whole, instead of its centre shown at full size with the edges cut off
+ * (SweetFramebuffer.cpp; touch follows, SweetHID.cpp). Boot-arg sweetfb_fit sets it at start.
+ */
+int sweet_fb_fit = 0;
+SYSCTL_INT(_kern, OID_AUTO, sweetfb_fit, CTLFLAG_RW | CTLFLAG_LOCKED, &sweet_fb_fit, 0,
+    "the presented display shrunk to fit the panel, whole");
 /* What the display showed (SweetFramebuffer.cpp counts them), for measuring the frame rate. */
 unsigned int sweet_fb_stat[4];
 SYSCTL_UINT(_kern, OID_AUTO, sweetfb_shown, CTLFLAG_RD | CTLFLAG_LOCKED, &sweet_fb_stat[0], 0,
